  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVEg">IV Eg</ref> 1a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1a" corresp="#wit-f">He beþohte ⁊ asmeade þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> godcunde be woruldgewunan:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1a" corresp="#wit-c">He beðohte ⁊ asmeade þæt godcunde be woruldgewunan:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1a" corresp="#wit-q">Ideo dignum memoria proferens exemplar ait:</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="1[b]" corresp="#wit-c">He beþohte ⁊ asmeade þæt godcunde be woruldgewunan:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-c">He has been thinking over and considering the ways of God by an analogy with human actions:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Er betrachtete und erwog das göttliche [Walten] gemäss weltlichem Gewohnheitsrecht:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">He considered and weighed the divine [order] by analogy with secular custom:</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann would supply ‘gerihta’ or ‘teoðunga’ or a synonym after ‘godcunde’.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
